  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Dark Utility Panel",
    "overview": "Pace ships as a near-black (dark default) or cool-grey (light) utility surface. Every screen is one column of hairline-bordered cards and rows set in Inter, with a single high-voltage lime accent for primary actions and a second, quieter indigo accent for state: the running activity, the current tab, the count badge, the focused composer. Color otherwise comes from a ten-hue \"project\" palette that appears only as small washed tags and outlined chips. Density is moderate: 44 to 56 px touch targets everywhere, a 4 px spacing grid, type mostly at 11 to 15 px. One React Native tree draws Android and the web (react-native-web); the only layout switch is the 1024 px \"wide\" breakpoint, where a 224 px sidebar and a 400 px detail pane appear.\n\nThe system is coherent at the token level (one JSON source, `packages/core/src/design/tokens.json`, mirrored into `--pace-*` CSS variables, with WCAG contrast pinned by `packages/core/src/design/contrast.test.ts`). It is weaker at the composition level. The owner's feedback concentrates there: the lime read as \"противно кислотный жёлтый\" (repulsively acid yellow) when it filled a full-width banner (`context/feedback-3.md:8-12`), \"два серых\" (two greys) side by side read as bad design (`feedback-3.md:62-64`), Day had dividers between some rows and not others (`feedback-4.md:121-124`), and the expanded composer was \"громоздкое\" (bulky) (`feedback-4.md:84-90`). Some of these are fixed in code at 057e484 (the update banner is now indigo, `apps/app/src/platform/update-banner.web.tsx:81`; status and importance tags now differ in hue, `packages/core/src/design/tokens.ts:71-88`). The underlying tendencies are still there: grey on grey, a hairline on every container, and lime as the default \"do it\" color.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Two themes from one token file; dark is the fallback when the OS gives no preference (`apps/app/src/platform/theme.ts:33-41`).",
      "Two accents: lime `accent` for primary actions, indigo `accentQuiet` for state and navigation.",
      "Ten project hues used only as 22 % washes under contrast-checked `ink-*` text, or as 2 px outlines.",
      "Flat tonal layering (`bg` < `surface` < `raised`) with 1 px `line` hairlines. Only two shadows exist (toast, wide dialog).",
      "Inter at weights 400, 500 and 600, Latin and Cyrillic, self-hosted on the web.",
      "Short fades (140 to 240 ms), plus one signature: a checked task dissolves into dust over 750 ms."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Two Accents Rule (incumbent)",
        "body": "Lime means \"do this\", indigo means \"this is on or here\". The code says it outright: \"lime is for the actions\" (`count-badge.tsx:4-5`).",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Washed Tag Rule (incumbent)",
        "body": "A project hue reaches text only through its `ink-*` shade over a 22 % wash of itself. Raw `project-*` hex never colors text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Family Rule (incumbent)",
        "body": "Inter everywhere, Cyrillic included. Nothing else ships.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline-On-Everything Rule (incumbent)",
        "body": "Containers separate by a 1 px `line` border, not by shadow or space. This is the source of the \"где-то есть черточки, где-то нет\" (dashes in some places, not in others) complaint (`feedback-4.md:124`) whenever a list mixes bordered and unbordered rows.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep every color in `packages/core/src/design/tokens.json` and reach it through `--pace-*` variables. The contrast test (`contrast.test.ts`) is the reason the incumbent passes AA in both themes.",
      "**Do** keep 44 px touch targets around visually smaller controls, as `CheckCircle` and `Chip` do.",
      "**Do** put hue on text only through an `ink-*` shade checked against its wash.",
      "**Do** keep Inter for Cyrillic as well as Latin (owner, `feedback-2.md`).",
      "**Do** keep each time-bar button large and in a fixed place (owner, `feedback-2.md`: \"каждая кнопка была довольно большой … и всегда находилась в своём месте\", every button fairly big and always in its own place)."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** spread the lime accent across large areas such as banners or bands. The owner called it \"противно кислотный жёлтый\" and asked for the palette to change (`feedback-3.md:8-15`).",
      "**Don't** put two neutral-grey tags side by side with different meanings (`feedback-3.md:62-64`: \"Плохой дизайн: два серых\", bad design: two greys).",
      "**Don't** mix bordered and unbordered rows in one list. Day's uneven dividers were rejected (`feedback-4.md:121-124`).",
      "**Don't** expand a quick-entry composer into a tall in-place form. The owner found it bulky and asked for it to move into the free right pane (`feedback-4.md:84-90`).",
      "**Don't** add a full-width button whose action is a no-op in the current state (a \"This week\" button while on this week, `feedback-4.md:114-117`)."
    ]
  }
